  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:5839",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside is implicated in the biological activity of U251 through a series of molecular interactions involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a target for multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A and a complex natural product, which in turn target U251. The evidence suggests that Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may exert its effects by modulating the proteasome pathway, potentially through the regulation of the 26S proteasome subunit 14. The presence of multiple target compounds and their shared interaction with the subunit indicates a possible mechanism of action involving the proteasome system. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the proteasome in mediating the biological effects of Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside, with U251 being a downstream effector in this process. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound interacts with the proteasome regulatory subunit, possibly influencing cellular processes through this pathway.",
